  "question": {
    "text": "In a collinear collision, a particle with an initial speed <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> strikes a stationary particle of the same mass. If the final total kinetic energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than the original kinetic energy, the magnitude of the relative velocity between the two particles, after the collision, is",
    "image": null
  },
